iated with this session have benefit start/stop dates and/or deduction start/stop dates that are earlier than the session open date. Please set the status to "Incomplete" and review the Deduction/Benefit Groups tab to modify the dates based on the session\'s plan year and pending effective date.',lstrhasFutureDateText="Has future date",lstrHeader="Header",lstrHeadOfHousehold="Head of Household",lstrHeadofHouseHoldMarriedCivilJointQualifyingWidowSurvivingPartnerRateB="Head of Household/Married/Civil Union Couple Joint/Qualifying Widow(er)/Surviving Civil Union Partner/Rate B",lstrHealthSavingsAccount="Health savings account",lstrHelp="Help",lstrHelpBtn="help - help for this page",lstrHelpForThisPage="Help for this page",lstrHide="Hide",lstrHideAll="Hide All",lstrHideDetails="Hide details",lstrHideMap="Hide Map",lstrHideMoreDetails="Hide more details",lstrHigh="High",lstrHighLowError="The values in the high cells must be greater than or equal to the values in the low cells",lstrHireAct2010ChoiceAMsg1="The Form W-11 should be received before saving this selection.\nThe option selected for 'HIRE Act 2010' indicates this employee is qualified for the New Hire Retention Credit only.\nIf applicable, an update may be made to adjust for Employer Social Security payments in prior payrolls if the employee was previously exempt. Adjustments for previous quarters will need to be filed manually.",lstrHireAct2010ChoiceAMsgA="The Form W-11 or equivalent form should be received before saving this selection.\nThe option selected indicates this employee will only be tracked for the New Hire Retention Credit and will still be subject to the Employer Social Security tax amount.",lstrHireAct2010ChoiceAorNMsgB="If this employee was qualified for the Employer Social Security exemption and has prior payrolls, then an update will be made to adjust the Employer Social Security tax amounts. If adjustments are applied to previous quarter(s), then a new quarterly tax file will need to be sent to